# Caddyfile — local HTTPS reverse proxy for Google OAuth development
#
# WHY WE NEED THIS:
#   Google OAuth requires a real domain in authorized redirect URIs.
#   localhost is NOT accepted for OAuth callbacks.
#   Caddy gives us https://app.nomadent.local with a valid local certificate.
#
# SETUP (one-time, do this before testing Google OAuth):
#
#   1. Download Caddy from https://caddyserver.com/download (Windows .exe)
#      and put it somewhere on your PATH (e.g. C:\caddy\caddy.exe)
#
#   2. Edit C:\Windows\System32\drivers\etc\hosts (run Notepad as Admin):
#        127.0.0.1   app.nomadent.local
#
#   3. Run Caddy (from the project root, where this Caddyfile is):
#        caddy run
#
#      On first run, Caddy will install a local root CA and auto-generate
#      a certificate for app.nomadent.local. Trust it when prompted.
#      (Or run: caddy trust)
#
#   4. Keep BOTH running simultaneously:
#        - npm run dev  → Next.js on localhost:3000
#        - caddy run    → Caddy proxy on https://app.nomadent.local:443
#
#   5. In Google Cloud Console:
#        Authorized JavaScript origins:
#          https://app.nomadent.local
#        Authorized redirect URIs:
#          https://app.nomadent.local/api/auth/callback/google
#
#   6. In .env.local:
#        NEXTAUTH_URL=https://app.nomadent.local
#
#   7. Visit https://app.nomadent.local instead of localhost:3000
#
# IMPORTANT: When done testing OAuth, you can revert NEXTAUTH_URL to
# http://localhost:3000 for normal development without Google OAuth.

app.nomadent.local {
  reverse_proxy localhost:3000
  tls internal
}
